  "question": {
    "text": "The specific heat capacity of a substance is temperature dependent and is given by the formula $C=k T$, where $k$ is a constant of suitable dimensions in SI units, and $T$ is the absolute temperature. If the heat required to raise the temperature of $1 \\mathrm{~kg}$ of the substance from $-73^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ to $27^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ is $n k$, the value of $n$ is _____\n[Given: $0 \\mathrm{~K}=-273^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$.]",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": 25000,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{T}_{\\mathrm{i}}=-73^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}=200 \\mathrm{~K} \\\\ & \\mathrm{~T}_{\\mathrm{f}}=27^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}=300 \\mathrm{~K}\\end{aligned}$\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{Q}=\\int \\mathrm{msdT} \\\\ & =\\int 1 \\cdot \\mathrm{kTdT} \\\\ & =\\int \\mathrm{kTdT}=\\mathrm{K} \\int_{200}^{300} \\mathrm{TdT} \\\\ & =\\frac{\\mathrm{K}}{2}\\left[\\mathrm{~T}^2\\right]_{200}^{300}=\\frac{\\mathrm{K}}{2}\\left[300^2-200^2\\right] \\\\ & \\mathrm{Q}=25000 \\mathrm{~K}\\end{aligned}$\nHence $n=25000$",
    "image": null
  },
